cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Argine2's data, code or findings, please cite the repository and the
  commit hash of the results you use, together with the EXP- identifiers.
title: "Argine2: expert memory as a resource-allocation problem in sparse MoE inference under a hard DRAM budget"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "sennape"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sennape/Argine2"
keywords:
  - Mixture-of-Experts
  - MoE inference
  - expert caching
  - expert offloading
  - expert streaming
  - NVMe inference
  - memory-tiered inference
  - llama.cpp
  - expert working set
  - routing concentration
  - online residency
abstract: >-
  An open, executable investigation of whether a fixed expert-memory budget should be
  allocated across MoE layers by measured marginal value rather than managed as a cache,
  on a 16 GB consumer PC streaming experts from NVMe through a hard-capped expert store
  in llama.cpp. Contains the runtime, research instrumentation, an event-atomic replay
  engine with offline oracles, committed historical raw measurement logs, processed
  experimental evidence, cryptographic metadata for the larger external raw trace corpus,
  and an experiment registry including
  falsified hypotheses.
